@@ -99 +103 @@ The current operation evidence is deliberately narrower than `*mut` parity:
-| other pointer casts, volatile intrinsics, effectful/scoped copies, atomics, references and allocation-dependent methods | require separate lowering, diagnostics and execution evidence |
+| other pointer casts, volatile intrinsics, effectful/scoped copies, atomics, references and allocation-dependent methods | remain outside the supported initial API and need separate lowering, diagnostics and execution evidence |
@@ -106,0 +111,7 @@ so 64-bit usize bounds diagnostics retain explicit unprintable placeholders.
+The negative method fixtures record the current pinned toolchain's diagnostics.
+They are not a promise that every optimization level diagnoses at the same
+helper, or that every unlisted raw-pointer operation is rejected. In particular,
+reference creation, in-bounds offsets and allocation-dependent operations are
+not part of the initial supported contract. Do not use a successful compile as
+proof that an unlisted operation has a sound host/shader ABI or runtime behavior.
